 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the vertices of the subgraph ",
 StyleBox["h", "TI"],
 " whose edges in ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " are all edges of ",
 StyleBox["h", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"ceb6cd73-008b-4b40-931c-264308dcfdb6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: the interior of a set ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 " of vertices of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " is int ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 " = {",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " \[Element] ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 " : every neighbour of ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " lies in ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 "}, the vertices whose closed ball of radius 1 lies in ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 ". It is ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 " less its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["GraphBoundary"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/GraphBoundary", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6f66e611-5863-4c7e-a6e8-6f3fcc9fa650"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4016848f-ca78-4ddf-9623-093721a1bf29"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The interior of an intersection is the intersection of the interiors, and a \
smaller set has a smaller interior. The interior of the ball of radius ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " contains the ball of radius ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " \[Minus] 1, and equals it where the graph goes on beyond the ball."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7afb8389-10e9-452c-b568-5cadd8c899df"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A subgraph ",
 StyleBox["h", "TI"],
 " is read with its own edges: a vertex of ",
 StyleBox["h", "TI"],
 " is interior when every edge of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " at it is an edge of ",
 StyleBox["h", "TI"],
 ". For an induced subgraph the two readings agree; a path has no interior."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4bf9d773-b5c9-4d60-b37b-daa365d5d7aa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraInterior"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraInterior", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "100b3292-cd11-4f7c-94a3-ce53cc5b97e2"],
 " with its default method is the interior of the vertex set, sorted; it \
reads a subgraph by its vertices. It is the interior of a closure space, not \
of a topology: taking the interior again shrinks the set again, while the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["TopologicalInterior"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/TopologicalInterior", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "703934f4-4419-4f33-83bd-72fb6a142be6"],
 " of the ball topology stays put."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f37e320a-6aa7-42ba-ae65-a0ff744b9e6e"]
}, Open  ]],

